# The push gate must check out with LF endings.
#
# core.autocrlf is true at system level on the operator's Windows box. Git's
# bundled MSYS sh happens to tolerate a CRLF shebang, so the hook survived a
# CRLF checkout when tested -- but that is one shell's implementation detail,
# not a guarantee, and the thing it would silently break is the push gate.
# Pin it rather than rely on the tolerance.
tools/hooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh           text eol=lf
